# The manifest of modules the process can load (docs/RUNTIME.md section 1.3).  Planner-owned.
#
#     <kind> <file name> [key=value ...]
#
#   lifted   a game DLL whose lifted C is linked into the program; the loader builds its
#            image from the DLL file.  Written as
#                lifted <file> dll=<path from the repository root> [module=<lifter module>] [dir=<guest dir>]
#            The generator reads the DLL and bakes its identity (size, PE timestamp,
#            SizeOfImage, SHA-256) into the row; the loader refuses any other file.
#            Lifted modules are NOT listed in this file: librt.a links no lifted code.  The
#            program that links a module's lifted C lists it in a file of its own in this
#            format and passes the generated table through RtConfig.extra_modules
#            (runtime/rt.mk, "lifted modules"; runtime/tests/abi/modules.def is the example).
#   system   a Windows DLL that exists only as shims (a native module)
#   stubbed  a game DLL we chose not to lift (a native module; a missing export is a trap stub)
#   exe      the native module standing in for the executable
#
# Order matters: bases are assigned in this order at start-up, 64 KB aligned with a 64 KB
# gap, lifted modules first and native modules after them (section 1.2), so every address
# of a build is the same in every run.  Add at the end of a group; do not reorder.
#
# Lifted modules get their bases first, in the order of the program's own list (see above).
# A lifted row written `place=late` is the exception: its base comes from the second half of
# the image arena (rt/module.h, RT_IMAGE_LATE_BASE), so adding it moves no base of this file.

exe      Titanfall2.exe

# ntdll.dll holds the runtime's own guest-visible code addresses (the return-to-host stub)
# and is what the C runtime asks GetModuleHandle for; no game DLL imports from it.
system   ntdll.dll

# The 26 libraries the 24 game DLLs import from (docs/findings/24-import-surface.md).
system   kernel32.dll
system   user32.dll
system   gdi32.dll
system   advapi32.dll
system   shell32.dll
system   ole32.dll
system   winmm.dll
system   ws2_32.dll
system   wsock32.dll
system   imm32.dll
system   bcrypt.dll
system   hid.dll
system   rpcrt4.dll
system   setupapi.dll
system   avrt.dll
system   psapi.dll
system   iphlpapi.dll
system   shlwapi.dll
system   opengl32.dll
system   avifil32.dll
system   d3d9.dll
system   d3d11.dll
system   msvcr110.dll
system   msvcp110.dll
system   gbclient.dll
system   mss64.dll

# Game DLLs that are stubbed instead of lifted (PLAN.md; OriginSDK until issue #32).
stubbed  GFSDK_SSAO.win64.dll
stubbed  GFSDK_TXAA.win64.dll
stubbed  OriginSDK.dll

# Microsoft's XInput 1.3 (the DirectX end-user runtime's; not a file of the install).  The
# input system's init loads it by name and treats a failed load as fatal
# (docs/handoff/gate3-run-2.md, entry 2).  Three functions, no controller connected
# (runtime/shims/xinput1_3/).  At the end, so that no other module's base moves.
system   XInput1_3.dll

# Microsoft's shader compiler library, shipped with the game and not lifted.  The material
# system imports two functions from it (finding 31, section 7): D3DReflect has a shim that
# answers from the shader's own bytes (runtime/shims/d3dcompiler_46/; unit d3d-reflect); any
# other export is a trap stub.  Until that unit the row stood at the end of gate3/modules.def,
# which follows this table in the order of bases: at the end here, no base moves.
stubbed  d3dcompiler_46.dll

# DirectSound, of which the game asks one function (DirectSoundCaptureCreate) for voice chat;
# it answers "no capture device" and the host's microphone is never opened (dsound-capture;
# runtime/shims/dsound/).  At the end of the file, so that no other module's base moves.
system   dsound.dll

# Microsoft's XAudio2 2.7 and the MMDevice API, which the game asks for by CoCreateInstance.  They
# exist to own these interfaces' vtables (runtime/com/interfaces.def, unit com-idl-source) and so
# that the game can load them by name; they have no shim.  At the end of the file, so that no
# other module's base moves.
system   xaudio2_7.dll
system   mmdevapi.dll
